  "question": {
    "text": "A biased die is marked with numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></math>&nbsp;on its faces and the probability of getting a face with mark&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>. If the die is thrown thrice, then the probability, that the sum of the numbers obtained is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn></math>, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>13</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>16</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>32</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>When we get the faces as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></math>&nbsp;then the probability will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>1024</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>When we get the faces as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;then the probability will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4096</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the required probability&nbsp;will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>1024</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4096</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>4096</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}